  "idea": "Some stocks are being quietly built up in ways that leave no mark on the price chart. Trading moves off the public exchanges. The people who run the company stop selling their own shares. And between one quarterly holdings report and the next, more big holders own the stock, or the ones who own it own more of it. Any one of those can happen by accident. This page tests what happens when all three point the same way at once, and it is graded against each one on its own, so the combination has to earn its place. One of the three readings is an absence: insiders not selling is treated as a reading in its own right.",
  "kill_criterion": "After 100 group names have been recorded and graded, if the three-way group's share reaching the top quarter adds less than 2 points over the best single condition on its own, this tool retires. Beating the plain all-stocks rate is not enough: the combination must beat its own best part.",
